# OpenAPI Generator Ignore — reviewed boilerplate trim list (Phase 77, SOW M3a, D-08).
#
# The `python` generator emits repo-management boilerplate alongside the client.
# The hazard is CI/tooling EXECUTING these scripts and workflows — not clutter —
# so each entry below states WHY it is dropped. Paths are relative to this
# directory (sdk/python), because openapi-generator reads this file from the
# output root (-o value). gitignore syntax; a `#` mid-line is literal, so every
# WHY comment sits on its own line above its entry.
#
# NO TYPESCRIPT-SIDE TWIN EXISTS: the typescript-fetch generator emits NONE of
# these files (verified live in 77-RESEARCH.md Pitfall 5), so typescript entries
# would be dead/misleading — D-08's review bar rejects dead entries.
#
# DELIBERATELY KEPT (do not add here): generated docs/ (feeds Phase 78 READMEs
# and Phase 79 guides) and generated test/ (seed for Phase 78 smoke), per D-08.

# WHY: pushes this directory to a remote git repo on execution — running it from
# inside this monorepo would create/force-push an unsanctioned external repo;
# publishing is Adi-gated (D-06/Phase 78) and never script-driven from output.
git_push.sh

# WHY: live Travis CI pipeline definition — if this tree is ever mirrored to a
# repo with Travis enabled, it would execute unreviewed third-party CI against
# our code. We define our own CI; generated pipelines must not run.
.travis.yml

# WHY: live GitLab CI pipeline definition — same execution hazard as .travis.yml
# for any GitLab-connected mirror. Unreviewed, not ours, must not run.
.gitlab-ci.yml

# WHY: nested GitHub Actions workflow — GitHub executes workflows from .github/
# directories; a mirror or subtree extraction of sdk/python would run this
# unreviewed workflow with the host repo's permissions. Our CI lives in the
# repo-root .github/ only.
.github/workflows/python.yml

# WHY: generator emits an EOL Python floor here (requires-python ">=3.9";
# 3.9 reached end-of-life 2025-10-31) that contradicts its own setup.py
# (">= 3.10") and README ("Python 3.10+"). No config knob exists to fix it
# (config-help -g python at 7.24.0 has no floor property), so this
# ignore-protected copy pins requires-python ">=3.10" as a D-21 named
# exception. This is packaging metadata, not API code — the reviewed
# exception mechanism, not a silent hand-edit (Phase 77-06, flagged to Adi).
pyproject.toml
